    "## 🎯 Fine-Tuning Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "### 📚 Key Principles\n",
    "1. **Lower Learning Rates** - Fine-tuning uses 2e-5 to 5e-5 (vs 1e-3 for training from scratch)\n",
    "2. **Gradient Clipping** - Prevents exploding gradients during fine-tuning\n",
    "3. **Task-Specific Heads** - Only the head is trained from scratch, BERT is fine-tuned\n",
    "4. **Proper Evaluation** - Use task-specific metrics (F1 for NER, EM for QA, etc.)\n",
    "\n",
